<p>
  <strong>In case you haven't looked yet:</strong> Remindly rings your parent's
  own phone, landline or mobile, when something is due (tablets, a glass of
  water, an appointment) and says it out loud. They press 1 when it's done. If
  there's a tablet in the house, it can speak from the screen instead. You set
  it all up from wherever you are, and for medication you get an email when a
  dose is marked done, or when the time passes and nobody marks it.
</p>

